  "id": "COMPOUND:29687 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Ampelopsin C is implicated in the regulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple indirect pathways, all of which converge on P-selectin glycoprotein ligand 1. This suggests that Ampelopsin C may act as a modulator of P-selectin glycoprotein ligand 1, which in turn targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. The presence of multiple distinct compounds—3,3-Diethoxy-1-propanol, hexacosyl (E)-3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)prop-2-enoate, and Retrojusticidin B—each acting as a target of P-selectin glycoprotein ligand 1, further supports the notion that Ampelopsin C may influence the activity of this receptor. The shared target of these compounds for Phosphodiesterase 6C indicates a potential role for Ampelopsin C in modulating the enzymatic activity of this enzyme, possibly through the regulation of P-selectin glycoprotein ligand 1. The evidence suggests a mechanistic link between Ampelopsin C and Phosphodiesterase 6C, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
